# Governance

{{ project_name }} belongs to {{ owner }}{% if license %}, under `{{ license }}`{% endif %}. This page says who does
what and how decisions are made.

## Roles

[//]: # "Maintainers: name each maintainer in the Who column, such as @octocat."

| Role | Who | Responsibilities |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Maintainer | The repository's owners | Sets direction, triages issues, reviews and merges {{ pr }}s, {% if ghlib %}approves each publication in the `nuget` environment, {% endif %}answers vulnerability reports, owns the repository's settings{% if library %} and the nuget.org packages{% endif %} |
| Contributor | Anyone | Opens issues and {{ pr }}s, under [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) and the [Code of Conduct](CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) |
| Automation | {% if review %}`ncode-review[bot]`, `ncode-review-approver[bot]`, {% endif %}Dependabot, GitHub Actions | {% if review %}Reviews and approves a clean pull request, as `ncode-review-approver[bot]` where NCode Review's approver is set up, whose approval meets the ruleset's required approval ([ADR-0036](docs/decisions/project-template/0036-a-required-approval-is-met-by-ncode-reviews-approver-app.md)), proposes dependency updates, runs CI, {% if ghlib %}tags and publishes releases{% else %}tags and publishes releases where `AGENTS.md`'s Landing section sets `release: tag+release`{% endif %}; never merges a pull request except the pin bump `code-review-auto-merge.yml` merges once the required checks pass and, where the ruleset requires an approval, it is approved: by `ncode-review-approver[bot]` after a clean review where NCode Review's approver is set up ([ADR-0041](docs/decisions/project-template/0041-ncode-review-reviews-and-approves-dependabots-pull-requests.md)), else by a maintainer{% else %}Proposes dependency updates, runs CI, {% if ghlib %}tags and publishes releases{% else %}tags and publishes releases where `AGENTS.md`'s Landing section sets `release: tag+release`{% endif %}; never merges a pull request{% endif %} |

Only a maintainer has write access. A contributor who keeps contributing reviewed, merged work can be invited to become
a maintainer; the existing maintainers decide, and the change is recorded in this file.

## Decisions

- Day-to-day decisions are made in issues and {{ pr }}s. Anyone can comment; a maintainer decides.
- A decision someone would otherwise re-argue is recorded as an architecture decision record in
  [docs/decisions/](docs/decisions/README.md), before or with the {{ pr }} that builds it. A change consumers can
  observe, such as to the public API, behavior or security posture, starts as an issue.
- Where maintainers disagree, they discuss it on the issue; with no agreement, the change doesn't happen.

## Releases

Versions follow Semantic Versioning. {% if ghlib %}Releases are tagged and published as
[ADR-0016](docs/decisions/project-template/0016-releases-are-tagged-and-published-when-their-pull-request-merges.md)
records.{% else %}Releases are tagged when `AGENTS.md`'s Landing section sets `release: tag`, and published too with
`tag+release`, as
[ADR-0016](docs/decisions/project-template/0016-releases-are-tagged-and-published-when-their-pull-request-merges.md)
records.{% endif %}
{%- if ghlib %} Packages reach nuget.org only after a maintainer approves the `nuget` environment.
[SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md) says how to verify a package.{% elif library and publisher %} The project's own workflow, `{{ publisher }}`, publishes the packages to nuget.org. [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md) says how to verify a package.{% endif %}

## Continuity

The repository, its issues, decision records, build, release automation and documentation are all in the
GitHub organization that owns it, so anyone given access can carry
on with no knowledge held elsewhere.
{%- if git_host == 'github' %} The organization's owners can administer every repository it holds, so they can step in
when the repository's maintainers can't.{% endif %}
{%- if ghlib %} nuget.org publishing uses trusted publishing, with no stored API key to hand over.{% elif library and publisher %} nuget.org publishing runs in `{{ publisher }}`: hand over whatever credential it uses with the repository.{% endif %}

[//]: # "Maintainers: name the owners, and keep the list current."

Owners today: the repository's owners{% if library %} and the owners of the nuget.org packages{% endif %}. Continuity
needs at least two people who can administer {% if library %}both{% else %}the repository{% endif %}; until there are
two, it is incomplete, and the OpenSSF Best Practices silver level can't be claimed
([docs/best-practices-badge.md](docs/best-practices-badge.md)).

